 "_comment": "Baseline seeding inputs for scripts/seed_baselines.py. A route's 12 monthly 'typical cheap round trip' figures = annual_level x shape[month]. This is the Charlotte methodology written down so it reproduces for every new origin instead of being re-guessed by hand each time.",
 "_shapes_note": "Normalised monthly multipliers (mean = 1.00). The first five were derived from the hand-seeded CLT curves in state/baselines.json (each curve divided by its own annual mean, then averaged within its group), so new cities inherit the same seasonality Charlotte was tuned to. 'europe' is hand-seeded: summer peak, deep Jan/Feb and November troughs. ADDED 2026-08-13 for the Charlotte destination expansion: 'latam' (Central and South America — mild, with a December peak because the southern summer and the holidays land together) and 'pacific' (long haul Asia/Pacific — northern summer peak plus a smaller year-end bump). Both are ESTIMATED shapes, hand-seeded the same way 'europe' was, and every route that uses them carries basis ESTIMATE and must stay labelled as one.",
